; Dogfooding the frozen snippet bytes (asm/docs/exec-abi-v1.md §16.3).
;
; Reads asm_oracle's Snippet_bytes table and asserts this assembler reproduces
; it from an AST. asm_oracle is the pure half of the oracle - constants and the
; recovery validator, no Unix - so this needs no toolchain and no emulator and
; runs in every leg that runs ppx_expect.
;
; The concrete target modules are named directly rather than reached through
; Driver.Registry, for test/coherence's reason: the types here are each target's
; own, so handing the aarch64 corpus an ARM operand is a compile error rather
; than a runtime one.
;
; ppx_expect, hence native only, and outside the production closure by
; construction - tools/asm-check-purity.sh classifies test/ as a non-production
; tree and rejects any production library that reaches it.

(library
 (name test_snippets)
 (modules snippet_ast test_snippets)
 (modes byte native)
 (libraries foundation target_intf asm_oracle x86_32 x86_64 arm aarch64 fmt)
 (inline_tests)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_expect))
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{env:ASM_MELANGE=false} true)))
